In article <rabram.56.744963509@unp4861.cc.unp.ac.za>, rabram@unp4861.cc.unp.ac.za (Rob Abrams) writes:
>Please could someone explain how to do the following,

Sure, I haven't done my civic duty (answering newbie questions) in a
while:

>
> - eat an item (e.g. ring etc...)

Polymorph into a monster which can eat metal (eg: a rust monster),
and just eat the way you normally do - the metalic rings (and other
metallic things) will appear in the list of things to eat (whether 
you're holding them or standing on them).  In version 3.1.1 or later,
this gives you a 1/3 chance of getting the intrinsic the ring gives.

To polymorph into a given monster, put on a ring of polymorph control
and (1) step into a polymorph trap or (2) zap yourself with a wand
of polymorph or (3) put on a ring of polymorph and wait, ...

Three monsters (rock moles, rust monsters, and Xorns) can eat metal
rings (pearl, iron, brass, copper, silver, gold, wire, engagement),
and gelatinous cubes can eat some non-metal rings (wooden, ivory).
The other rings can't be eaten.

> - name a weapon

Naming a weapon isn't all that useful.  The powerful artifacts can't
be made this way.  Only Sting (an elven dagger) and Orcrist (an elven
broadsword) can be made by naming.  You won't be allowed to just name 
a long sword Excalibur (try it).  Anyhow, to name a weapon (on my 
system anyway) you type "Ny" or "#ny".

To get better weapons, try sacrificing fresh corpses (repeatedly) on
an altar to your god.
> 
>Also what is an Elbereth ???

Comes from the Lord of the Rings (it's the name of an elven queen). 
In nethack, if you Enscribe the name on the ground, some monsters
will not attack you while you stand on it (until it gets wiped off).
Wands of Fire, magic markers, athames, and a few other things are 
very good for engraving.
